Clinical Course: The confusion and breathing difficulty are direct results of the infection. The hospital will provide oxygen and strong antibiotics to clear the lung and restore normal brain function over the coming days.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

(Directed to nursing staff): An ambulance has been dispatched. Do not attempt to lay the patient flat. Ensure their medical chart and advanced care directive are ready for the paramedics.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: (Directed to family/staff): He has developed a severe pneumonia, which is a bacterial infection filling the lower right side of his lung with fluid. This infection has entered his bloodstream, causing the high fever and severe confusion. He needs hospital-level care immediately for intravenous antibiotics and oxygen to survive this infection.
Actionable Steps: Keep him sitting upright to help him breathe. Prepare his documentation for the ambulance transfer.

